6. The scalar rule on uniform weights: the rule clips on the side opposite to the largest entry
   The largest entry goes to level -q/2 and the levels stop at q/2 - 1. A weight within half a step of the far end is pulled back a whole level.
   Its squared error is 7/12 of a squared step in the mean, not 1/12. A uniform weight is there with chance 1 / (2 q). So the error is 1 + 3/q times the formula's.
   group | rate | levels q | measured over formula, dB | 10 log10(1 + 3/q)
